NetXMS licensing

NetXMS source code has mixed licensing. Most libraries are licensed under the
GNU Lesser General Public License, and the rest of the NetXMS components under
the GNU General Public License. Third-party libraries and code fragments
bundled with the source tree carry their own licenses, listed at the end.

Abbreviations used below:

  GPL    GNU General Public License version 2, or (at your option) any later
         version. Full text in GPL.txt.
  LGPL   GNU Lesser General Public License version 3, or (at your option) any
         later version. Full text in LGPL.txt.

Each source file carries its own license notice. Where a notice and this list
disagree, the notice in the file applies.


Libraries

  libnetxms        LGPL    core utility library
  libnxsl          LGPL    NXSL script interpreter
  libnxdb          LGPL    database abstraction layer
  libnxsnmp        LGPL    SNMP protocol
  libnxlp          LGPL    log parser
  libnxsrv         LGPL    shared server-side code
  libnxagent       LGPL    shared agent-side code
  libnxclient      LGPL    C client library
  libnxnetconf     LGPL    NETCONF client
  libethernetip    LGPL    EtherNet/IP client
  libnxjava        LGPL    Java bridge, C++ part; org.netxms.bridge
                           Java classes GPL
  libnxmb          GPL     message bus
  libnxsde         GPL     structured data extractor
  libnxtux         GPL     Tuxedo helper
  libnxdbmgr       GPL     shared code of nxdbmgr


